    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="21">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Wi">Wi</ref> 21</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-h"><seg type="part" corresp="#part-a"><pb n="14" ed="#liebermann"/>ceorlisc man hine feowra sum his heafodgemacene on weofode;</seg> <seg type="part" corresp="#part-b"><pb n="14" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ ðissa ealra að sie unlegnæ.</seg></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><seg type="part" corresp="#part-a"><pb n="28" ed="#attenborough"/>Ceorlisc man hine feowra sum his heafodgemacene on weofode;</seg> <seg type="part" corresp="#part-b"><pb n="28" ed="#attenborough"/>⁊ ðissa ealra að sie unlegnæ.</seg></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#oliver" corresp="#wit-h" n="16.1–16.2"><seg type="part" n="16.1" corresp="#part-a"><pb n="158" ed="#oliver"/>Ceorlisc man hine feowra sum his heafodgemacene on weofode;</seg> <seg type="part" n="16.2" corresp="#part-b"><pb n="158" ed="#oliver"/>⁊ ðissa ealra að sie unlegnæ.</seg></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><seg type="part" corresp="#part-a"><pb n="14" ed="#liebermann"/>Ein gemeinfreier Mann [reinige<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Wi_21-a.lnote.de.1"/>] sich als einer von vieren<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Wi_21-a.lnote.de.2"/> seiner Standesgenossen am Altar;</seg> <seg type="part" corresp="#part-b"><pb n="14" ed="#liebermann"/>und dieser<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Wi_21-b.lnote.de.3"/> aller Eid sei untadelig.</seg></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman"><seg type="part" corresp="#part-a">A common freeman [is to clear] himself as one of four of his equals in rank at the altar;</seg> <seg type="part" corresp="#part-b">and the oath of all these is to be unimpeachable.</seg></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><seg type="part" corresp="#part-a"><pb n="29" ed="#attenborough"/>A commoner may clear himself at the altar, with three of his own class;</seg> <seg type="part" corresp="#part-b"><pb n="29" ed="#attenborough"/>and the oath of all these [collectively] shall be incontrovertible.</seg></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock" corresp="#wit-h"><seg type="part" corresp="#part-a"><pb n="398" ed="#whitelock"/>a <hi rend="italic">ceorl</hi> with three of the same class on the altar; and the oath of all these is to be incontrovertible. 2 1.. Then the Church’s right of exculpation is as follows:</seg></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#oliver" corresp="#wit-h"><seg type="part" corresp="#part-a"><pb n="159" ed="#oliver"/>A man of freeman rank as one of four of his equals at the altar;</seg> <seg type="part" corresp="#part-b"><pb n="159" ed="#oliver"/>and let the oath of all these be incontrovertible.</seg></ab>
        <note type="concordance"><seg type="edition">Oliver 16.1, 16.2</seg></note>
        <note type="translator" source="#whitelock" target="#part-a">Here and in the following chapters, the word translated “servant” is esne. see p. 393, n. 8.</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#whitelock" target="#part-a">Whitelock translates Wi 21 as one clause, which the sheet divides into rows 21[a], 21[b]; her translation of the whole is given here, in the first row.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Wi_21-a.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">29</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ellipse wie <hi rend="italic">o.</hi> 11²</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Ellipsis as <hi rend="italic">above</hi> 11²</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Wi_21-a.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">29</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. o.</hi> 19²; hieraus Emendationsvorschlag Hl 5⁹</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. above</hi> 19²; hence the proposed emendation at Hl 5⁹</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Wi_21-b.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">29</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Der in 17—21 erwähnten. Zu <hi rend="italic">unlegen</hi> <hi rend="italic">s. o.</hi> 16⁴</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Of those mentioned in 17—21. On <hi rend="italic">unlegen</hi> <hi rend="italic">see above</hi> 16⁴</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
  </text>
